The '''2022 [[Sheffield City Council]] election''' took place on 5 May 2022 to elect members of Sheffield City Council in England, as part of the [[2022 United Kingdom local elections|nationwide local elections]]. One seat from each ward was up for election.

This was the first election held since the formation of a Labour-Green coalition in 2021,<ref>{{cite web |title=Sheffield City Council: Labour and Green coalition to run authority |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/uk-england-south-yorkshire-57175934 |website=[[BBC]] |access-date=12 April 2022 |date=12 April 2022}}</ref> following the loss of Labour's overall majority on the council. Following the election, the council remains under No Overall Control.

